    "result_text": "Done. The full configured test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`) passes \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures/errors.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a derived DTO field computed in `OwnerMapper` from values stored on the `Owner` entity \u2014 exactly the pattern the existing `namesakeCount` rule already uses (a small AOP aspect stamps a count onto the owner just before save, and the mapper reads it). I mirrored that pattern rather than growing anything:\n\n1. **`OwnerHouseholdSizeAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained `@Before` aspect that, on create, counts existing owners sharing the same `householdId` and stores `existing + 1` as the household size. It derives the household key with the *exact* UUID computation the mapper uses for `householdId`, so \"same householdId\" is honored precisely.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `householdSize` field plus its getter/setter (CC-1 each), next to `namesakeCount`.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 prepended one GOLD branch to the `membershipTier` expression: `householdSize >= 3 \u2192 GOLD`, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE ternary is untouched.\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `household_size` column and padded the 10 seed rows (required because the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`; h2 auto-updates and mysql/postgres schemas \u2014 like `namesake_count` before them \u2014 are only maintained for hsqldb here).\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n\n- The mapper edit is a **single line**; that method's CC is 1 and its class has small `WMC_other`.\n- New behaviour lives in a **fresh small class** with near-zero surrounding complexity, rather than expanding `OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice`, the service, or the controller.\n- The `Owner` additions are trivial CC-1 accessors.\n- No existing method grew in complexity; the frozen-at-create snapshot avoids injecting a repository into the mapper (which would have forced a riskier interface\u2192abstract-class conversion and touched call sites).",
